# Qtech Service Hub - always-on project rules

## Stack and folders
- npm workspaces: apps/server (Express, Prisma, PostgreSQL), apps/web (Vite,
  React, Tailwind, TanStack), packages/shared (@app/shared, TS source).
- Server modules: apps/server/src/modules/<name>/{routes,service,schema}.ts.
  Web features: apps/web/src/features/<name>. One place per concept:
  permissions and roles in shared/permissions + shared/roles, metric
  definitions in shared/metrics, constants in shared/constants.
- Database: PostgreSQL localhost:2001, database qtech_service_hub, via Prisma.
  Ports: web 5173, server 4000. The web app calls /api through the Vite proxy.

## Coding rules
- TypeScript strict, no any, no dead code, no TODOs, no obvious comments.
- ONLY code and required config. NO test files, mocks, seed data, README, docs.
  Temporary verification scripts must be deleted afterwards.
- No unrelated refactors. Do not rename existing API routes.
- Every screen: skeleton matching the final layout, empty state, error state.
  Every mutation: pending state, success feedback, failure message.

## API contract
- All routes under /api, JSON only (except file upload/download).
- Errors: { error, code, requestId, details? }. Codes/status: VALIDATION 400,
  UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, NOT_FOUND 404, CONFLICT 409,
  PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE 413, RATE_LIMITED 429, INTERNAL 500. 500 only for real
  bugs. Missing or expired session is 401, never 500.
- Wrap every async handler. Validate every body/query/param with zod.
- Multi-table writes use one prisma.$transaction (row change + mirrored fields
  + ActivityLog together).
- Side effects (notifications, outbox, SSE, publishEvent) NEVER make the main
  write fail: catch and log them separately.
- Auth cookie qsh_session: httpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure only when
  COOKIE_SECURE=true. DB stores only the sha256 of the token. requireAuth
  re-checks user.active on every request.

## Data and time
- Dates over the wire: YYYY-MM-DD for date-only, ISO 8601 for instants.
  "Today" = current date in APP_TIMEZONE (one helper). Display dates like
  "07 Apr 2023" and times like "12 Oct 2026, 4:32 PM". Excel dates are read
  with UTC components (no off-by-one).
- Row.data (JSON) is the source of truth; mirrored columns on Row are updated
  in the same transaction as every write and are used for all filters,
  metrics and counts. Time-dependent flags (overdue, due, expired, expiring)
  are computed at query time and never stored.

## Roles and capabilities (fixed, not configurable)
- admin: everything. users, access matrix, import/merge, edit any cell, row
  add/insert/duplicate/delete, column+group add/rename/move/hide/delete,
  dataset delete, Trash restore and permanent delete, verify, assign.
- manager: everything above EXCEPT users, access matrix, permanent delete.
- validator, service: only edit cells of groups where RoleGroupAccess.canEdit,
  plus their own actions. NEVER: import, row or column or group changes, dataset
  delete, Trash, Users, Access, Schema.
- Capability names: manageUsers, manageAccess, importData, editAnyCell,
  manageRows, manageStructure, deleteDataset, useTrash, purgeTrash, verify,
  assign.
- Actions: validate (validator, manager, admin; validator also needs edit on
  data_validation); amc / pms / followup (service, manager, admin; need edit on
  amc / schedule_services / follow_up); calls (service, manager, admin; need
  edit on complaint or breakdown_calls); verify and assign (manager, admin).

## Group access defaults (validator / service), stored in RoleGroupAccess
customer_detail: both view. instrument_details: both view. data_validation:
validator view+edit, service hidden. schedule_services, complaint,
breakdown_calls, amc, follow_up: service view+edit, validator hidden. Any other
or custom group: hidden for validator and service until an admin ticks it.
canEdit implies canView. groupKey is immutable; renaming changes only the
label. Admin and manager always have full view+edit.

## Hidden means hidden (server enforced)
For validator/service the API never returns values, labels, columns, activity
entries, notification field names, search hits or export cells of groups
without canView. Search, filters, sorting and counts run only on visible
data. The UI removes (never merely disables) what a role lacks. Derived pills
workflows need (verified, warranty, AMC lead) may remain visible as computed
pills.

## Server-managed fields (nobody can type into them; only actions/derivations)
validated (after Task 6), validated_by, validated_at, verified, verified_by,
verified_at, amc_status, ack_at, warranty_live, days, next_due_pms, open_calls,
last_call_date, assigned*.

## Domain definitions (one shared metrics module; computed at query time)
- needs_validation: validated empty.
- validation_overdue: validated No AND validation_due < today.
- pending_verification: validated Yes AND verified != "Verified OK".
- warranty_expired: end_date < today. expiring_soon: within EXPIRING_DAYS.
- Effective AMC status: stored Proposal Sent / Acknowledged / Declined, else
  expired -> "AMC Due", otherwise "Not Due".
- amc_due: warranty_expired AND effective status "AMC Due" AND (when
  AMC_REQUIRES_VERIFICATION) verified = "Verified OK". Admin/manager also see
  an "Unverified expiries" list.
- Active AMCs: effective status Acknowledged.
- contract_live: end_date empty or >= today. next_due_pms: earliest scheduled
  real date (pms:N) whose pm_date:N is empty (mirrored to Row.nextDuePms).
  pms_overdue: contract_live AND nextDuePms < today. pms_due_soon: contract_live
  AND nextDuePms within PMS_SOON_DAYS. Assumption: pms:N = scheduled date,
  pm_date:N = date actually done. Expired-contract rows show PMS as "Lapsed"
  and are excluded from PMS KPIs, agendas and reminders.
- followup_due: next_follow_up <= today.
- days = end_date - start_date in whole days (server computed, read-only,
  blank if either missing, negative in ruby).

## Constants (packages/shared/src/constants.ts)
DAILY_VALIDATION_TARGET=20, RECENT_EDIT_HOURS=24, UNDO_SECONDS=8,
NOTIFY_MERGE_SECONDS=60, TRASH_RETENTION_DAYS=30, EXPIRING_DAYS=30,
PMS_SOON_DAYS=3, AMC_REQUIRES_VERIFICATION=true, MAX_UPLOAD_MB=25,
MAX_ROWS=10000.

## Domain events
Every successful write calls publishEvent({ type, datasetId?, rowId?, actorId,
... }). Subscribers (realtime, notifications) are added in Task 7.

## Design system: Executive Ivory (quiet luxury, restraint is the luxury)
- Variables: canvas #FAF9F7, surface #FFFFFF, surface-2 #F4F2EE, hairline
  #E8E4DD, ink #14171F, ink-2 #4A4F5C, muted #7B7F8B, navy #0E1726 (sidebar,
  primary buttons), navy-2 #172236, gold #B8955A (ONLY accent: focus ring,
  active tab underline, selected outline, nav indicator, edit markers, small
  icons), gold-soft #F3EBDD. Pills (text/bg): emerald #1F6F4F/#E6F2EC, amber
  #96620F/#FBF0DA, ruby #A63A38/#F8E6E5, sapphire #2A5698/#E6EDF8, stone
  #5C616D/#EEEDEA. Group tints: #F1EEE8 #E9EFEA #E8EDF3 #F3ECE3 #EFE9EF #E6EFEE
  #F1EBE6 #ECEBF3.
- Type: "Instrument Serif" only for page titles, big numerals, login. "Inter"
  elsewhere (13px tables, 14px UI, tabular-nums for numbers and dates). Group
  labels 11px uppercase, tracking 0.06em. Fonts self-hosted.
- Cards radius 12, controls radius 8, 1px hairline, no shadow at rest;
  floating layers only get a soft shadow. Primary button navy with ivory text;
  secondary white with hairline; gold is never a large fill. Motion 160ms ease;
  respect prefers-reduced-motion. Styled checkboxes, selects, date pickers (no
  raw browser controls). Empty states: one-color line illustration + one
  sentence + one action. Toasts bottom-right (top on mobile), navy.
- Forbidden: neon or saturated colors, gradients, glassmorphism, emojis, mixed
  icon sets, shadows everywhere, small gold text on white, more than one accent.
  Body text contrast >= 4.5:1. One icon set (lucide, 1.5px stroke).

## Layout laws (hard rules)
- Shell is a CSS grid: sidebar | main. Main = topbar 56px + scrollable content.
  Only the content area scrolls vertically. The PAGE never scrolls horizontally
  from 320px up; wide tables scroll inside their own container.
- Flex/grid children holding text get min-w-0 plus truncate/line-clamp. No fixed
  widths on text containers. Content max-width 1440px; padding 32 desktop / 24
  tablet / 16 mobile.
- z-index variables only: base 0, sticky 10, topbar 20, scrim 40, drawer 50,
  popover 60, dialog 70, toast 80. Popovers, dialogs, dropdowns, tooltips,
  drawers, toasts render in portals. No ad-hoc z-index values.
- Sticky offsets from CSS variables (--topbar-h, --banner-h, --subheader-h).
- Drawers OVERLAY with a scrim and never push content: 480px (max 92vw); full
  screen sheet with a sticky bottom action bar on mobile.
- Breakpoints: >=1280 desktop (sidebar 232px); 768-1279 tablet (64px icon rail
  that expands as an overlay); <768 mobile (no sidebar, bottom nav max 5 items,
  tables become card lists, dialogs become bottom sheets).
- 44px minimum tap targets on touch; hover-only actions need a touch
  alternative. 8px spacing scale; card padding 20; gaps 16/24. One PageHeader
  pattern: serif title 28px, one-line subtitle, actions on the right (wrapping
  below on small screens). Skeletons match final dimensions.

## Definition of done for every task
Run typecheck, lint and build and fix everything you introduced. Run the app and
exercise the task's VERIFY list (curl and the running UI). Fix failures. Delete
temporary scripts. Then STOP, print "Task N complete" with changed files and
manual steps, and wait for me to say "continue". Never start the next task
alone.
